{"name":"Homoeopathic Orange","hex":"#f2e6e1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"homoeopathic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative spelling of homeopathic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/homoeopathic"},{"term":"orange","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen tree of the genus Citrus such as Citrus sinensis which yields oranges (the fruit).","Any round citrus fruit with a yellow-red colour when ripe and a sour-sweet taste; the fruit of the orange tree.\n Specifically, a sweet orange or Citrus sinensis."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the colour of the fruit of an orange tree; yellowred; reddish-yellow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orange"}],"entries":[{"title":"Homeopathy","blocks":[{"text":"Homeopathy or homoeopathy is a pseudoscientific system of alternative medicine. It was conceived in 1796 by the German physician Samuel Hahnemann. Its practitioners, called homeopaths or homeopathic physicians, believe that a substance that causes symptoms of a disease in healthy people can cure similar symptoms in sick people; this doctrine is called similia similibus curentur, or \"like cures like\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Saxonia_Museum_fuer_saechsische_Vaterlandskunde_III_19.jpg/330px-Saxonia_Museum_fuer_saechsische_Vaterlandskunde_III_19.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homeopathy","wikidata":"Q81058"},{"title":"Orange (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange is the colour between yellow and red on the spectrum of visible light. The human eyes perceive orange when observing light with a dominant wavelength between roughly 585 and 620 nanometres. In traditional colour theory, it is a secondary colour of pigments, produced by mixing yellow and red. In the RGB colour model, it is a tertiary colour. It is named after the fruit of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Delicatearch.png/330px-Delicatearch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_(colour)","wikidata":"Q39338"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Homeopathy-2.jpg/500px-Homeopathy-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Homeopathy-2.jpg/1280px-Homeopathy-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Homeopathy-2.jpg/500px-Homeopathy-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHomeopathy-2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Samuel_Hahnemann_Monument%2C_Scott_Circle.jpg/500px-Samuel_Hahnemann_Monument%2C_Scott_Circle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Samuel_Hahnemann_Monument%2C_Scott_Circle.jpg/1280px-Samuel_Hahnemann_Monument%2C_Scott_Circle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Samuel_Hahnemann_Monument%2C_Scott_Circle.jpg/500px-Samuel_Hahnemann_Monument%2C_Scott_Circle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Samuel Hahnemann Monument, Washington, D.C., with the inscription Similia Similibus Curentur – \"Like cures Like\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASamuel_Hahnemann_Monument%2C_Scott_Circle.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Homeopathy_Looks_at_the_Horrors_of_Allopathy.jpg/500px-Homeopathy_Looks_at_the_Horrors_of_Allopathy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaig